<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 03:04:44 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>几个世纪前，皇室成员打扮他们的玩偶来分享最新的时尚。了解芭比娃娃、娃娃和其他小型潮流引领者如何为设计师带来灵感</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/centuries-ago-royals-dressed-up-their-dolls-to-share-latest-fashions-see-how-barbies-baby-dolls-and-other-tiny-trendsetters-have-inspired-designers-ever-since-180989580/</link><description>纽约市 FIT 博物馆举办的新展览展示了 170 多件物品，这些物品追溯了玩偶与时尚之间经常出乎意料的关系</description><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:22:29 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/centuries-ago-royals-dressed-up-their-dolls-to-share-latest-fashions-see-how-barbies-baby-dolls-and-other-tiny-trendsetters-have-inspired-designers-ever-since-180989580/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，由于巨大的胃和被盗的基因，这种巨大的深海不倒翁可以在没有食物的情况下生存数年</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-massive-deep-sea-roly-poly-can-go-years-without-food-thanks-to-a-huge-stomach-and-a-stolen-gene-study-suggests-180989562/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，巨型等足类动物 Bathynomus jamesi（一种类似巨大药丸虫的海底生物）的祖先在 1600 万年前从细菌中获得了 DNA 片段。该基因帮助动物减缓新陈代谢</description><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:53:41 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-massive-deep-sea-roly-poly-can-go-years-without-food-thanks-to-a-huge-stomach-and-a-stolen-gene-study-suggests-180989562/</guid></item><item><title>考古学家挖掘出有 2,400 年历史的学校，亚里士多德曾在这里教导亚历山大如何变得伟大</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-unearth-the-2400-year-old-school-where-aristotle-taught-alexander-to-be-great-180989581/</link><description>位于古代米耶扎的亚里士多德体育馆的最新发掘揭示了华丽的马赛克大厅，研究人员相信亚历山大大帝在这里学习了他的成长课程</description><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:49:38 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-unearth-the-2400-year-old-school-where-aristotle-taught-alexander-to-be-great-180989581/</guid></item><item><title>卫星图像显示格陵兰岛和南极洲在过去 50 年中损失了超过 12 万亿吨冰</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/satellite-images-reveal-greenland-and-antarctica-have-lost-more-than-12-trillion-tons-of-ice-over-the-past-50-years-180989567/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，大部分冰冻水已经消失，因为冰川流入海洋的速度更快，而不是因为冰盖表面融化。研究人员估计冰损失已使全球海平面上升一英寸以上</description><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:36:55 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/satellite-images-reveal-greenland-and-antarctica-have-lost-more-than-12-trillion-tons-of-ice-over-the-past-50-years-180989567/</guid></item><item><title>来认识一下“火变形虫”，这是一种新发现的斑点生物，它的复杂生命能承受多少热量，超出了人们的预期</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-the-fire-amoeba-a-newfound-blobby-organism-thats-defying-expectations-about-how-much-heat-complex-life-can-handle-180989557/</link><description>根据一项新的研究，在北加州拉森火山国家公园发现的新描述的物种仍然可以在 145 华氏度的温度下繁殖，并在 147 华氏度的温度下移动</description><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-the-fire-amoeba-a-newfound-blobby-organism-thats-defying-expectations-about-how-much-heat-complex-life-can-handle-180989557/</guid></item><item><title>在图坦卡蒙国王陵墓之外发现了神秘的“异常现象”。它们可能是通往失踪已久的纳芙蒂蒂王后遗骸的秘密通道吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mysterious-anomalies-have-been-detected-beyond-king-tuts-tomb-could-they-be-secret-passageways-leading-to-the-long-lost-remains-of-queen-nefertiti-180989576/</link><description>地球物理调查为埃及法老被埋葬在现有墓葬群的外室的理论提供了新的证据。研究人员正试图获得批准自行调查</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:08:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mysterious-anomalies-have-been-detected-beyond-king-tuts-tomb-could-they-be-secret-passageways-leading-to-the-long-lost-remains-of-queen-nefertiti-180989576/</guid></item><item><title>首次发现海龟在美国西海岸筑巢。科学家称“超级”厄尔尼诺现象可能将他们带到那里</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-a-first-sea-turtles-were-spotted-nesting-on-the-us-west-coast-scientists-say-the-super-el-nino-could-have-brought-them-there-180989574/</link><description>九月份，人们发现两只橄榄丽龟在南加州的海滩上产卵。在太平洋，这些爬行动物通常在更南的地方筑巢，通常在墨西哥、尼加拉瓜、哥斯达黎加和巴拿马</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:24:20 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-a-first-sea-turtles-were-spotted-nesting-on-the-us-west-coast-scientists-say-the-super-el-nino-could-have-brought-them-there-180989574/</guid></item><item><title>希特勒与他同父异母的侄女有着密切而神秘的关系。新研究表明他谋杀她的不在场证明可能站不住脚</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/hitler-had-an-intense-mysterious-relationship-with-his-half-niece-new-research-suggests-his-alibi-for-her-murder-might-not-hold-up-180989572/</link><description>最近发现的有关吉莉·劳巴尔死亡时间的文件对这位纳粹领导人的不在场证据提出了新的怀疑，近一个世纪以来，该证据一直被认为是相当合理的</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:07:56 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/hitler-had-an-intense-mysterious-relationship-with-his-half-niece-new-research-suggests-his-alibi-for-her-murder-might-not-hold-up-180989572/</guid></item><item><title>澳大利亚发现了两种新的竹节虫物种，另一种则隐藏在众目睽睽之下</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-new-stick-insect-species-have-been-discovered-in-australiaand-another-one-was-hiding-in-plain-sight-180989575/</link><description>新发现强调，即使在有大量观测的地区，科学家们对于昆虫多样性还有很多需要了解的地方</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:03:30 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-new-stick-insect-species-have-been-discovered-in-australiaand-another-one-was-hiding-in-plain-sight-180989575/</guid></item><item><title>科学家发明了一种可消化的纸基电池，可为吞咽或植入的医疗设备供电</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-invent-a-digestible-paper-based-battery-that-can-power-swallowed-or-implanted-medical-devices-180989549/</link><description>到目前为止，该技术仅在猪身上进行了测试。如果它在人类身上取得成功，有一天它可能会成为监测您健康状况或在体内输送药物或电流的电动工具</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:37:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-invent-a-digestible-paper-based-battery-that-can-power-swallowed-or-implanted-medical-devices-180989549/</guid></item><item><title>两千多年前，朱利叶斯·凯撒征服了最终成为巴黎的定居点。考古学家可能刚刚发现它</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-thousand-years-ago-julius-caesar-conquered-the-settlement-that-eventually-became-paris-archaeologists-may-have-just-found-it-180989569/</link><description>在塞纳河西岱岛的一家医院进行挖掘时，研究人员发现了可能曾经保护过卢泰西亚（法国首都的高卢前身）的城墙的一部分</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-thousand-years-ago-julius-caesar-conquered-the-settlement-that-eventually-became-paris-archaeologists-may-have-just-found-it-180989569/</guid></item><item><title>蝙蝠起源于哪里？大规模的基因研究可能解决了长期存在的争论并改写了生物的进化树</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/where-did-bats-originate-huge-genetic-study-may-have-settled-the-longstanding-debate-and-rewritten-the-creatures-evolutionary-tree-180989568/</link><description>根据这项新研究，飞行哺乳动物可能出现在 6500 万年前的欧洲，然后传播到非洲，然后传播到世界其他地方</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/where-did-bats-originate-huge-genetic-study-may-have-settled-the-longstanding-debate-and-rewritten-the-creatures-evolutionary-tree-180989568/</guid></item><item><title>参观刚刚归还希腊的一系列令人惊叹的被盗希腊文物，跨越 5000 年历史</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-a-stunning-collection-of-stolen-greek-artifacts-spanning-5000-years-that-were-just-returned-to-greece-180989566/</link><description>曼哈顿地区检察官小阿尔文·布拉格 (Alvin L. Bragg Jr.) 办公室的调查人员在大都会艺术博物馆没收了这些古董。</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-a-stunning-collection-of-stolen-greek-artifacts-spanning-5000-years-that-were-just-returned-to-greece-180989566/</guid></item><item><title>有些鸟鸣声比其他鸟鸣声更悦耳。对我们来说，更高音调、复杂的声音往往听起来更美妙</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/some-birdsongs-are-more-pleasing-to-human-ears-than-others-higher-pitched-complex-calls-tend-to-sound-more-beautiful-to-us-180989540/</link><description>在一项新研究中，超过 80 名参与者对 123 种欧洲鸟类发出的声音的悦耳程度进行了评分。然后研究人员研究了最受欢迎和最不受欢迎的歌曲的音质</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:01:33 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/some-birdsongs-are-more-pleasing-to-human-ears-than-others-higher-pitched-complex-calls-tend-to-sound-more-beautiful-to-us-180989540/</guid></item><item><title>在古埃及堡垒中发现了拥有 3000 年历史的战马墓葬和拉美西斯二世石碑等文物</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-3000-year-old-warhorse-burial-and-a-ramses-ii-tablet-among-other-relics-have-been-discovered-in-an-ancient-egyptian-fortress-180989564/</link><description>尼罗河三角洲的新发掘提供了有关新王国时代军事和居住生活的令人大开眼界的线索</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:07:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-3000-year-old-warhorse-burial-and-a-ramses-ii-tablet-among-other-relics-have-been-discovered-in-an-ancient-egyptian-fortress-180989564/</guid></item><item><title>为什么克劳德·莫奈一遍又一遍地画同样的场景？这位印象派艺术家痴迷于捕捉时间的转瞬即逝的本质</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-did-claude-monet-paint-the-same-scenes-over-and-over-again-the-impressionist-artist-was-obsessed-with-capturing-the-fleeting-nature-of-time-180989563/</link><description>泰特现代美术馆即将举办的展览将展出莫奈在 1870 年代至 1920 年代创作的 60 多件艺术作品。这些作品揭示了他如何记录不断变化的光线和天气条件</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:01:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-did-claude-monet-paint-the-same-scenes-over-and-over-again-the-impressionist-artist-was-obsessed-with-capturing-the-fleeting-nature-of-time-180989563/</guid></item><item><title>科学家表示，“超级”厄尔尼诺现象带来的灼热气温到二月份可能会导致近50万人死亡</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-say-scorching-temperatures-brought-on-by-the-super-el-nino-could-kill-nearly-half-a-million-people-by-february-180989555/</link><description>预测数字包括六月以来的死亡人数，可能低估了总死亡人数。炎热天气可能会持续到二月之后，气候变化可能会带来其他危及生命的情况，包括洪水、野火和传染病</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-say-scorching-temperatures-brought-on-by-the-super-el-nino-could-kill-nearly-half-a-million-people-by-february-180989555/</guid></item><item><title>一位金属探测器在德国勘探时惊讶地发现了大量罗马硬币</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-metal-detectorist-exploring-a-field-in-germany-was-stunned-to-discover-a-massive-hoard-of-roman-coins-180989561/</link><description>943 枚第纳尔银币跨越了从公元前 148 年到公元 124 或 125 年近 300 年的罗马历史</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-metal-detectorist-exploring-a-field-in-germany-was-stunned-to-discover-a-massive-hoard-of-roman-coins-180989561/</guid></item><item><title>这幅来源神秘的立体派绘画在芝加哥艺术博物馆悬挂了数十年。现在，博物馆将把它归还给合法的犹太继承人</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-cubist-painting-with-a-mysterious-provenance-hung-in-the-art-institute-of-chicago-for-decades-now-the-museum-will-return-it-to-its-rightful-jewish-heirs-180989553/</link><description>红外成像将 20 世纪 Jean Metzinger 的作品与一位收藏家联系起来，该收藏家的作品在二战期间被纳粹命令强制拍卖</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:18:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-cubist-painting-with-a-mysterious-provenance-hung-in-the-art-institute-of-chicago-for-decades-now-the-museum-will-return-it-to-its-rightful-jewish-heirs-180989553/</guid></item><item><title>土耳其研究人员出土了一块刻有世界上最古老和平条约的古代碎片</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-in-turkey-have-unearthed-an-ancient-fragment-inscribed-with-the-worlds-oldest-peace-treaty-180989554/</link><description>这块泥板刻有阿卡德楔形文字，其文字属于古埃及人和赫梯人于公元前 13 世纪签订的《卡迭石和平条约》</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:39:01 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-in-turkey-have-unearthed-an-ancient-fragment-inscribed-with-the-worlds-oldest-peace-treaty-180989554/</guid></item></channel></rss>